# Left and right margins: DECLRMM (mode 69) and DECSLRM, and what they limit.
#
# In several cases all four rows hold "abcdefghij" and the margins are columns 3 to 6 ("cdef").

test DECSLRM sets the margins and homes the cursor
spec VT510 DECSLRM: moves the cursor to column 1, line 1; recognized only if DECLRMM is set
known-fail: alacritty – DECLRMM (mode 69) is not supported: DECRQM answers 0 and CSI Pl ; Pr s sets no margins
size 10 4
feed \e[?69h\e[1;1H\e[3;4H\e[3;6s
cursor 1,1

test DECSLRM is not recognized without DECLRMM
spec VT510 DECSLRM: the terminal only recognizes this control function if DECLRMM is set
size 10 4
feed \e[1;5H\e[3;6s\e[9C
cursor 1,10

test the right margin stops cursor forward
spec VT100 User Guide CUF: the cursor stops at the right margin
known-fail: alacritty – DECLRMM (mode 69) is not supported: DECRQM answers 0 and CSI Pl ; Pr s sets no margins
size 10 4
feed \e[?69h\e[3;6s\e[1;4H\e[9C
cursor 1,6

test the left margin stops cursor backward
spec VT100 User Guide CUB: the cursor stops at the left margin
known-fail: alacritty – DECLRMM (mode 69) is not supported: DECRQM answers 0 and CSI Pl ; Pr s sets no margins
size 10 4
feed \e[?69h\e[3;6s\e[1;5H\e[9D
cursor 1,3

test backspace at the left margin does nothing
spec VT510 Table 4-1 BS: if the cursor is at the left margin, no action occurs
known-fail: alacritty – DECLRMM (mode 69) is not supported: DECRQM answers 0 and CSI Pl ; Pr s sets no margins
size 10 4
feed \e[?69h\e[3;6s\e[1;3H\b
cursor 1,3

test carriage return goes to the left margin
spec VT510 Table 4-1 CR: moves the cursor to the left margin on the current line
